## Problem

Task operators cannot reliably filter sandbox failure alerts by backend when a run continues or the agent reports the failure.

## Changes

- Continued runs retain the backend of their attached sandbox when the rollout flag changes.
- Agent and workflow failure events identify the backend when known. Failures before backend selection remain untagged.
- Older continuation payloads infer Modal from an attached sandbox without a provider stamp.

Before:

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A[Continue run] --> B[Re-evaluate rollout flag] --> C[Label failure]
    classDef phBlue fill:#1d4aff,stroke:#1d4aff,color:#fff;
    classDef phYellow fill:#f9bd2b,stroke:#f9bd2b,color:#000;
    class A,C phYellow;
    class B phBlue;
```

After:

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A[Continue run] --> B[Use attached sandbox backend] --> C[Label failure]
    classDef phBlue fill:#1d4aff,stroke:#1d4aff,color:#fff;
    classDef phYellow fill:#f9bd2b,stroke:#f9bd2b,color:#000;
    class A,C phYellow;
    class B phBlue;
```

## Problem

- An agent bump PR waits for a person when any of the six sandbox images fails to build.
- It waits even when the base image built and passed its agent smoke.
- On #106231 (agent 2.4.224), the pi image hit an npm 404 for an AWS SDK tarball published 3 minutes earlier ([image build run](https://github.com/PostHog/posthog/actions/runs/36044984574)).
- The bump workflow reads `Sandbox Base Image Pass`, which covers all six images, so it stopped before the Go ai-gateway smoke ran ([bump run](https://github.com/PostHog/posthog/actions/runs/36044136794)).

## Changes

- The bump now waits for a new `Sandbox Base Image Smoke` check. It passes only when the base image built and its packaging smoke passed.
- The packaging smoke now runs whenever the base build succeeds. Before, a notebook or streamlit failure in the same parallel group skipped it.
- `Sandbox Base Image Pass` is unchanged. It still covers all six images and is still not a required check.
- The error message and the Slack text name the new check. This part is mechanical.

Before:

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    base[Base image build] --> smoke[Packaging smoke]
    others[notebook, streamlit, pi, autoresearch, vm] --> pass[Sandbox Base Image Pass]
    smoke --> pass
    pass --> bump[Bump workflow]
    bump --> gw[Go ai-gateway smoke]
    gw --> approve([Approve and enqueue])
    classDef phBlue fill:#1d4aff,stroke:#1d4aff,color:#fff;
    classDef phRed fill:#f54e00,stroke:#f54e00,color:#fff;
    classDef phYellow fill:#f9bd2b,stroke:#f9bd2b,color:#000;
    classDef phGray fill:#e5e7eb,stroke:#c7ccd1,color:#000;
    class base,smoke,pass,bump phBlue;
    class others phGray;
    class gw phRed;
    class approve phYellow;
```

After:

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    base[Base image build] --> smoke[Packaging smoke]
    smoke --> gate[Sandbox Base Image Smoke]
    others[notebook, streamlit, pi, autoresearch, vm] --> pass[Sandbox Base Image Pass]
    smoke --> pass
    gate --> bump[Bump workflow]
    bump --> gw[Go ai-gateway smoke]
    gw --> approve([Approve and enqueue])
    classDef phBlue fill:#1d4aff,stroke:#1d4aff,color:#fff;
    classDef phRed fill:#f54e00,stroke:#f54e00,color:#fff;
    classDef phYellow fill:#f9bd2b,stroke:#f9bd2b,color:#000;
    classDef phGray fill:#e5e7eb,stroke:#c7ccd1,color:#000;
    class base,smoke,gate,bump phBlue;
    class others,pass phGray;
    class gw phRed;
    class approve phYellow;
```

| Image build failure | Before | After |
| --- | --- | --- |
| pi, autoresearch or vm | Waits for a person | Runs the gateway smoke |
| notebook or streamlit | Waits for a person | Runs the gateway smoke |
| Base build or packaging smoke | Waits for a person | Waits for a person |
